#!/bin/bash
#PBS -N cgm_push
#PBS -P 11704243
#PBS -j oe
#   qsub -l select=1:ncpus=8:mem=32gb -l walltime=00:30:00 \
#        -o logs/98_push_report.log scripts/pbs/98_push_report.pbs            # -> qdev
source "${REPO:-$HOME/workspace/Project_CGM/CGM-OutlierMIA-master}/scripts/pbs/env.sh"
set +e
module load git/2.39.2
cd "$REPO"
{
  git add -A
  echo "staged: $(git diff --cached --numstat | wc -l) files"
  git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'
Both pilots finish. One is unreadable, and a decision chain so the record stays followable

TWO-CHANNEL, 21/21 AT h128 AND 40,000 STEPS -- NOT READABLE. Eight discriminator
restarts on the base give max 0.9408 with a spread of 0.3908: the bimodal signature of
a generator that did not fit, the same one that condemned the seven-day h96 line. Its
arm AUC of 0.820 cannot be interpreted. A second tell was there: the joint distance
reads 0.820 while CGM alone reads 0.370 and basal alone 0.600, and a joint far ABOVE
both parts is backwards.

The 40,000-step budget was cut from the published 100,000 on my recommendation, because
this cohort's loss is flat from 20k. That inference was wrong. A converged loss says the
objective stopped improving; it says nothing about whether a classifier can separate the
samples. The abandoned 100k attempt was moved aside rather than deleted, so its
80,000-step checkpoint is being resampled and scored to tell the step cut apart from the
second channel.

SEVEN-DAY h256, 21/21 -- QUALITY PASSES AND THE EFFECT IS LARGE. Restart max 0.624,
spread 0.068, tight rather than bimodal. Arm AUC 0.950 (p = 0.0004); per-subject outlier
0.628 against control 0.459; six of ten outliers above 0.55 and none of ten controls;
1142 at 1.000.

It is not yet evidence about window length. 22,000 steps over 7,001 windows is 201
epochs against the published run's 36, so the seven-day models saw each training window
5.5x more often. Window length and training regime are still tangled, and a full
three-replicate design at 50,000 steps would cost 1,449 GPU.h to measure the wrong thing.

So the control comes first: the same 573 subjects, the same design, 6,996 ONE-DAY
windows, the same 22,000 steps and the same hidden_size 256, so only T differs. 8 GPU.h.
Running.

Housekeeping: the seven-day h96 line is deleted -- 7.6 GB across three runs, config and
meta kept as stubs. Its restart distributions survive as the failed-generator comparator
and are labelled as that rather than as a seven-day result, because without a condition
known to be separable a tight distribution at 0.55 could just mean the discriminator
never works on this data.

MEMO.md now opens with a decision chain: one row per decision, the observation that
forced it, and what it made us do next. HISTORY, SUMMARY_CN and MEMO together run to
fifteen thousand words and none of them answered "why that next".

The notebook's per-day counts are now ARTEFACTS ONLY (results/ and data/cohort/). Logs
move when a rerun overwrites them, and docs/scripts/src carry "last edited" rather than
"written that day", so a count including them could never settle -- it drifted twice
while the checker was running. 138 checks against the artefacts, 0 mismatches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
MSG
  git log --oneline -1
  git -c credential.helper="store --file=$HOME/.git-credentials-github" \
      push origin main 2>&1 | sed -E 's#//[^@]*@#//***@#g'
  echo "push exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
} 2>&1 | tee logs/98_push_report.live.log
